      "title": "Money in, money out",
      "body": "In your club, The Rotary Foundation (TRF) has two sides:\n\n**Money out**: grants for your club projects\n- **District Grants** are managed by the District Foundation Committee. They are for smaller local or international projects, to be finished within the Rotary year.\n- **Global Grants** can fund larger projects overseas or in Australia. The minimum size is **US$30,000**, and there are extra requirements, including a community assessment.\n\n**Money in**: donations to TRF from your club and your members\n- All clubs are expected to make an annual donation to TRF. The district handbook recommends **US$100 per member** (check the current district figure).\n- Separately, clubs are encouraged to support **PolioPlus**, Rotary's flagship cause.\n- Your **club Foundation Chair** encourages personal giving and makes sure donors are properly recognised.\n\n> To qualify for any TRF grant, a member of your club must attend the **Grants Seminar** (held in May)."
